1
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:09,177
Why him, of all people?

2
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:10,780
What was Father thinking?

3
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:14,377
Giving a man of unknown
lineage the Black Blade?

4
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:17,225
It was from back when
Father was an adventurer.

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,897
He and the Sovereign
Six had pushed deep into

6
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:22,657
the darkest corner of
the Dungeon of the Lost.

7
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:28,557
It was a long and dangerous quest that,
upon exiting, yielded a prime dungeon relic.

8
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:29,897
That Blade is the most powerful.

9
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,817
Made of an unknown material
harder than mithril

10
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:36,877
or a calcum or even
monometal no matter the

11
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:39,797
technique or skill used
nothing can cause even

12
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:43,297
a scratch upon it it
has become known as the

13
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:47,517
unbreakable blade the
biggest question is given

14
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,117
its resilience how could
such an indestructible

15
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:54,297
material gotten so
beaten up that sword has

16
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:57,860
value beyond that of a
weapon how could he just?

17
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:01,717
let such a thing go.

18
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:04,697
No, I'm thinking about this wrong.

19
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:06,898
Father has also noticed the sense of

20
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:09,637
unrest hanging over the country.

21
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:13,760
In all likelihood, he is
putting his faith in that man.

22
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:21,020
The one who defeated a rampaging
minotaur and saved Lin's life.

23
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:24,977
He might very well be
our secret weapon for

24
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:27,472
whatever is sure to happen in the future.

25
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,460
Oh, wait, Lynn.

26
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:37,180
Can you be seen out here in public? Yes.

27
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:39,714
First and foremost, I am an adventurer.

28
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:41,730
Um, well, okay.

29
00:01:41,813 --> 00:01:44,617
I'm thinking we should go
to the guild after we eat.

30
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,000
That sounds terrific, instructor.

31
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:49,520
Oh, man.

32
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,877
I'm really not the type
of guy who should be

33
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:54,057
considered capable enough
of instructing Anybody?

34
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:54,970
Anything?

35
00:01:55,053 --> 00:01:59,460
How did everything get so complicated
and she just follows me around

36
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,037
everywhere all the time?

37
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,897
Once I get some real work from the guild,

38
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,677
she'll finally be able to
grasp how clueless I am

39
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:10,197
out there and drop this
whole instructor nonsense?

40
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:12,217
I hope that you can find.

41
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:14,300
a befitting task soon, Instructor!

42
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:15,880
Let's eat!

43
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:47,200
For every moment, the truth is not
allowed to be able to afford anything.

44
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:50,237
What can I have for you?

45
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,520
What can I have for you?

46
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:57,640
I can't take it away from my heart,
but I will never be able to get back.

47
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:03,537
Even if it is a dream,

48
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:09,017
I'm not allowed to go back.

49
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:12,280
I'm not allowed to be able to get it.

50
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,544
Thank you so much for watching.

51
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:50,980
Noor, why are you here
with Lady Lindbergh?

52
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,220
Master! Huh?

53
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,877
As an adventurer, I go by the name Lin.

54
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:57,489
No need to add any titles.

55
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,280
Uh, okay.

56
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:00,519
My apologies, Lin.

57
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,920
Hey, what's all this, Noor?

58
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:05,517
Did anything else happen to you yesterday?

59
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:09,120
Oh, well, uh, it's kind of
difficult to explain. Hmm?

60
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:16,297
Well, one of our rules is not sticking
your nose where it doesn't belong.

61
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,420
Forget I asked.

62
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:20,300
Oh, I was hoping he'd give me some advice.

63
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,386
So, what brings you in today?

64
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:23,580
Looking for work?

65
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:24,880
Oh, uh, yeah.

66
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:27,137
One that two people can do, if possible.

67
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:29,620
A two-person job, huh? Hmm.

68
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:35,800
So if I remember correctly,
you're Silver B-Ring, right? Yes!

69
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:42,017
If you two form a party together, you
can take on the goblin hunting job?

70
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:43,982
in the outskirts of the capital.

71
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,030
Oh, man!

72
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:47,120
A goblin hunting job?

73
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:50,497
Goblins are the monsters
that adventurers all over

74
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:53,404
the world fight to put
their skills to the test.

75
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:57,520
Wait, sir, can we really take
on an adventure like that? Yeah.

76
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:01,277
Lynn can accept silver tasks
like this all on her own,

77
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:03,297
but bringing along a partner like you?

78
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:06,145
with a lower rank than
hers is a big liability.

79
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:09,575
Normally, the job will drop
down a rank or two, though.

80
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,500
I don't believe this! A quest!

81
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:13,120
Outside the castle!

82
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:14,560
Whoa, hold it.

83
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:18,157
This means I'm completely taking
advantage of Lin's adventurer rank.

84
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,380
And let's be real.

85
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:23,073
Up until now, all I've wanted
is for her to go back home.

86
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:28,600
She sees right through me.

87
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:31,840
I'm such a scumbag, and she knows it.

88
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:35,620
Even so, she does still want to be here.

89
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:36,780
All the time.

90
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,806
Um, what's wrong, Instructor?

91
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:40,320
Well, yeah.

92
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,097
Sure you're okay with this?

93
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:43,560
I mean, as it is,

94
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:47,760
I'm relying solely on your rank to
take on this goblin hunting job.

95
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:49,700
Of course I'm okay with it!

96
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:53,757
If there's anything I can do for
you, just say the word, alright?

97
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:54,940
Oh, seriously?

98
00:05:56,440 --> 00:06:00,080
Yes, I do feel kind of bad for
using her status to get ahead.

99
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:03,940
But hey, one of my lifelong
dreams is finally coming true!

100
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:08,477
Alright, we're heading out!

101
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:11,854
Wait, I haven't told you where
you're going or anything.

102
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,380
Oh, yeah, right.

103
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:17,551
But you want to take it anyway, don't you?

104
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,020
Well, of course.

105
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,360
Now don't go nuts out there.

106
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:27,120
A low threat level doesn't mean that
it's easy peasy, okay? Don't you worry.

107
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:29,301
I'm well aware of my limitations.

108
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,000
You're going to this area here.

109
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,580
Only report what you catch.

110
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,400
That's the Forest of Beast. Correct.

111
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:40,497
The right ear will be the
proof of your success.

112
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:42,756
You won't be getting paid without it.

113
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,680
So be sure to bring it back. Understood.

114
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,551
Bring back the right ear.

115
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:51,317
So there have been reports of their
numbers diminishing quite a bit lately.

116
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:55,137
If you don't come across one, then go
ahead and pick some medicinal herbs.

117
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:56,050
Right.

118
00:06:56,133 --> 00:06:57,460
Now go on, get on with it.

119
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:59,462
And I'm serious, don't get hurt.

120
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:01,140
And here we go.

121
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:08,960
Open the gate!

122
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,420
Adventure onward! Right! Sure thing!

123
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,520
So we are in the Forest of the Beasts.

124
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:32,237
The trees are getting
pretty dense, aren't they?

125
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:36,557
These are different types of plants than
what we see in the southern forests.

126
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,557
They're gargantuan.

127
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:40,140
The ecological system here is very unique.

128
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,951
Yeah, you're not kidding.

129
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:51,700
Lynn, what kind of
creatures are goblins? What?

130
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:55,680
I mean, I'd like to at least
hear about them beforehand. Sure.

131
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:58,737
Normally they hunt small animals as prey?

132
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:00,377
And eat the fruits off trees,

133
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:03,754
but they've been attacking
humans for sustenance lately.

134
00:08:04,140 --> 00:08:05,477
If we leave them be,

135
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:10,097
their numbers grow too large which leads
to a food shortage which in turn would

136
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,377
overflow into human villages.

137
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:13,577
That's why adventurers
are regularly dispatched

138
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,597
to hunt them and control their numbers.

139
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,510
Control them?

140
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:19,197
The health of the ecological
system of the forest

141
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,868
actually depends on
whether or not there are

142
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:25,917
goblins, which means we don't want
to hunt them to extinction either.

143
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:30,588
Also, this forest has rare flora and
fauna that are not found in other places,

144
00:08:30,740 --> 00:08:32,858
so it's Sometimes used for training,

145
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,668
for beginner adventurers
to forage and hunt.

146
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,120
Good to know.

147
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:42,700
Not only does Lynn have the skills,
she knows all sorts of... stuff.

148
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:45,515
What can I possibly teach this person?

149
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,497
You got anything?

150
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:04,877
Afraid not? None here? Either?

151
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,457
That's strange. Right?

152
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:10,757
Under normal circumstances, we would
have encountered a few of them already.

153
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:14,900
I suppose the rumors
about the goblin numbers.

154
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:18,697
dwindling are true.

155
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:21,057
I'm getting something from
a creature to the northwest.

156
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:24,600
I'll pinpoint its location.
So we found one? Yes.

157
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:27,687
It shouldn't take too
much time to get there.

158
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,135
Let's go take a look.

159
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,377
It keeps getting darker and darker.

160
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:37,284
There are some extremely
old trees in this area.

161
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,437
Makes it hard for the
sun to shine through.

162
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:43,217
Goblins are known to
prefer a place like this.

163
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:44,535
Of course they would.

164
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:45,850
Huh?

165
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:47,990
What's wrong?

166
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:52,077
The presence of a monster was right
up ahead, but all of a sudden...

167
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:53,580
It disappeared.

168
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,900
It's gone? Yes.

169
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,957
Monsters are living beings like us, right?

170
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:03,637
So you think that they can maybe
just die from illness or old age?

171
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:06,480
Um, yeah, I guess that
could be a possibility.

172
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,160
It was around here!

173
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:17,580
I don't see anything.

174
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,220
Yeah, me neither.

175
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:24,940
No, wait. Hold on.

176
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,680
What is that?

177
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:39,740
Uncover!

178
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:49,860
Wait, what is that?

179
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,920
It's a goblin.

180
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,500
A big one, too.

181
00:10:58,020 --> 00:11:00,160
So that's a goblin?

182
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:02,600
It's way bigger than I imagined.

183
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,677
They're said to be one of the weakest,

184
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:09,407
but there's a huge difference in hearing
about it and meeting one face to face.

185
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:13,817
The gnarly beast has all
the calling cards green

186
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:17,640
skin walking on two legs
piercing glowing eyes.

187
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:22,220
And they use tools.

188
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:31,577
I'll bet all you higher ranked adventurers
handle these guys like they're nothing.

189
00:11:31,660 --> 00:11:32,577
Huh?

190
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:33,657
Okay.

191
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:35,017
So she's freaked out.

192
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:37,057
She may be blessed with abilities but...

193
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:39,787
She has very little
actual combat experience.

194
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:42,537
You don't need to be frightened.

195
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:44,460
We're only up against a goblin.

196
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:50,580
Terrifying, but worry about that later.

197
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:53,130
We got this.

198
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,600
Right, let's go!

199
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:03,460
I'm covered!

200
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:16,177
This is...

201
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:17,640
it can't be...

202
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,720
No, it's the Goblin Emperor.

203
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:25,520
A subspecies of the Goblin King,
considered an extreme threat.

204
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:30,292
The Goblin Emperor is a beast created
from genetic manipulation by mankind.

205
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:31,850
In fact,

206
00:12:31,933 --> 00:12:34,817
the deviant research that brought forth
this forbidden knowledge is now banned.

207
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:37,720
On top of that, this
one eats its own kind,

208
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:40,277
ingesting their power and
growing even stronger.

209
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,877
You don't need to be frightened.

210
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,784
We're only up against a goblin.

211
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:47,250
Wait a minute.

212
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:49,652
Did Nor come here because of this goblin?

213
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:53,437
He was so excited to take
on this job because he

214
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:56,579
wanted to eliminate a threat
no one else knew about.

215
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,372
I've got your back, Lin.

216
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,130
That's right.

217
00:13:01,213 --> 00:13:02,620
I am not alone.

218
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:07,080
Right!

219
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:08,220
Let's go!

220
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,110
Perry!

221
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:21,700
Perry!

222
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,120
Trying to corner me?

223
00:13:33,380 --> 00:13:35,560
Nah, I ain't gonna let that happen.

224
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,120
Lynn! On it!

225
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:44,040
Full windcutter!

226
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,160
Icicle dance!

227
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:53,520
I can't hit him!

228
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,918
I didn't think it could be so quick!

229
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:01,630
Perry!

230
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:06,730
Instructor!

231
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:07,677
Are you alright?

232
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:08,590
Look out!

233
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:17,380
Perry! Perry!

234
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:18,933
I have to do something!

235
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:26,750
Huh?

236
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:27,663
Hang on.

237
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:28,920
Where's the wound?

238
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:32,575
Goblin emperors shouldn't be
able to recover so easily.

239
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,700
That's it! Instructor!

240
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:38,509
The stone on its forehead!

241
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:41,151
If you can get that off, we can defeat it!

242
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:48,020
No way!

243
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,593
He was watching how many I could handle.

244
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:53,660
I can't block them all.

245
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:56,070
Windblast!

246
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:06,720
Are you okay?

247
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:08,250
Yeah.

248
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:11,220
I knew it.

249
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:18,440
It's constantly replenishing
its power with the monostone.

250
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:26,406
If we keep fighting like this, we're going
to run out of both stamina and magic.

251
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:30,617
But if your magic attacks aren't
able to hit them and keep them down,

252
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,700
nothing I can do is going to work.

253
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:34,850
Hey, Lin.

254
00:15:34,933 --> 00:15:36,719
Can you aim that attack at my back?

255
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,270
Wait, what?

256
00:15:38,353 --> 00:15:40,040
You mean windblast? Yeah.

257
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:50,597
That move is powerful enough
to demolish Castle Balls.

258
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,417
You don't possibly want me to...

259
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:53,735
I think I'll be okay.

260
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:57,380
I have this to protect me.

261
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:01,795
Our only chance of getting
out of here is to be faster.

262
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:04,530
Okay.

263
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:10,700
Here we go. Let her rip.

264
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,380
Full weight loss. Fast!

265
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,115
Physical enhancement.

266
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:25,750
Feather steps.

267
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:31,190
Low heel.

268
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:02,310
Instructor!

269
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:03,820
Where's the stone?

270
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:05,061
It's right here.

271
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:12,300
Lynn, can you be the one to finish it off?

272
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:16,309
And please don't let it suffer
any more than it already has.

273
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:18,280
Yes, of course I can.

274
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:35,080
Hellfire!

275
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:38,460
Hellfire!

276
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:01,480
I'm sorry, goblin.

277
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:07,499
I think I'll refrain from any more
goblin slaying for the time being.

278
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:13,460
I was way overconfident and got
into too many dangerous situations.

279
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:19,940
I'll have to do a lot more training
before taking on the next challenge.

280
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,740
So it was a goblin emperor, huh?

281
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:34,181
It must have been quite powerful.

282
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:37,760
With this size monostone,
it's larger than normal.

283
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:42,574
According to the reports, it was
several times the size of a goblin king.

284
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:43,940
I'm sure it was.

285
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:46,560
The size is unusual.

286
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:50,580
The Magic Empire may be
responsible for the event itself.

287
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:52,980
But still, this stone, though.

288
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:58,560
We think, sir, it could be a demon's
heart from the holy theocracy of Mithra.

289
00:18:59,020 --> 00:18:59,850
How is Lin?

290
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,900
Only minor wounds.

291
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:05,040
It must have been a terribly hard battle.

292
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,557
It's amazing they were able to survive.

293
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:10,937
The monster itself hid
behind a powerful seal

294
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:13,600
and ambushed them in the forest of beasts.

295
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:16,697
The lady believes it had
been there a few days,

296
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:20,540
and in fact, maybe even
more than that. A few days?

297
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:24,546
So this seal is one that not even
the secret core can perceive.

298
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:27,557
But how are they transporting such a bulky

299
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:30,077
thing all the way here in the first place?

300
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:32,060
If they use summoning magic,

301
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:34,737
the sensory network in the
capital should have caught it.

302
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:37,120
Did nothing show up in the perimeter?

303
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:39,937
The number of goblins was decreasing,

304
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:43,608
so the Adventurer's Guild
requested an investigation into it.

305
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:47,904
There may have been several similar
cases in other areas as well.

306
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:53,228
This report is a summary of questionable
instances from the last three months.

307
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:57,175
Well done, gentlemen.

308
00:19:58,060 --> 00:19:59,589
Continue with the inquiry.

309
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:01,517
Well, look at you.

310
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,897
I never thought that the little runt from

311
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:06,297
way back when would
grow up to slay goblins?

312
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,997
It was so much nastier
that I thought it would be.

313
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:14,020
But Lynn came in at the last moment and we
managed to get the job done. No problem.

314
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:16,260
Oh, no, that's not how it went

315
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:22,837
It happened my very first
hunt I should celebrate

316
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:25,397
it may be just another
quest to other adventurers.

317
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:29,760
But to me this is you know
everything you did well?

318
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:34,197
Best to just watch from the
sidelines and let her handle it.

319
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:37,339
And I guess probably it's
the wiser choice, too, eh?

320
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:38,370
You know what?

321
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:41,377
I'm just grateful I got to
help her out a little bit.

322
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:44,636
I have no idea where I'd be
if Lynn hadn't been there.

323
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:48,320
But I'm the one that just
helped you out, remember?

324
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:52,678
Well, even goblins can still be a
threat to newbies from time to time.

325
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,808
But it was a good
experience for you, right?

326
00:20:56,220 --> 00:20:57,537
Exactly, it certainly was.

327
00:20:57,620 --> 00:21:02,091
Until I saw one in real life, I had no
idea goblins were anything like that.

328
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:05,497
And who knew about the stone on
its forehead being a weak point?

329
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:06,992
A stone on the forehead?

330
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,477
What are you talking about?

331
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:10,637
Yeah, kind of a shiny reddish color.

332
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,426
And kind of pretty, actually.

333
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:15,140
Oh, you mean a monostone.

334
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:18,124
It's normally buried in
the heart or the throat.

335
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:19,770
Hmm.

336
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:22,620
Are you sure that was
really a goblin, my boy?

337
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:24,217
Yeah, well, of course.

338
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:26,000
A goblin, right? Indeed.

339
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:28,317
If that's what you say it is, instructor,

340
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:31,165
then that is that, no
matter what anybody says.

341
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:34,336
Might have been a rare type, I guess.

342
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:38,449
All right, let's see
the proof of the kill.

343
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:40,628
I'm going to get your cash.

344
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:44,160
The right ear?

345
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:46,694
I told you to bring back the right ear?

346
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,460
No way.

347
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,800
Um, we might have set that goblin on fire.

348
00:21:58,260 --> 00:21:59,280
You did what?

349
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:23,560
Oh?

350
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:07,920
Oh!
